# Where to buy, cart, and gold chest

**$$$** (Where to buy), the green **cart**, and the Dumpers-gold **loot chest** are one combined tool. Adding, removing, or updating one of them on a surface updates the others that belong on that surface. Patch day refreshes the loot tables and every bake these icons read, in the same run.

## What each icon means

| Icon | Shows when | Data |
|---|---|---|
| $$$ and cart | The item has at least one shop with a buy price | `shopItemForBlueprint` / `shopItemForLoot` in `src/lib/uexCatalog.ts` |
| Gold chest | The item is in at least one tracked Loot Finder location | `game-site-loot.json` via `lootItemForEntityClass` |

A missing shop row means the item is not sold. Do not invent a shop. The chest stays when any tracked location still lists the item.

## Patch day (all of these, every patch)

| Bake | Command | Icons it feeds |
|---|---|---|
| Loot tables | `npm run parse-game-data` (or `npm run bake-site-loot` for loot-only) → `src/data/game-site-loot.json` | Gold chest, Loot Finder lists |
| Personal shops | `npm run fetch-shop-item-index` → `shop-item-index.json` | $$$ and cart for guns, ammo, armor, clothing, medpens, food, drinks, plushies |
| Ship shops | `npm run fetch-ship-shop-shops` after parse → `ship-shop-shops.json` | $$$ and cart for ships and ship parts |
| Mining gear | `npm run fetch-mining-gear-shops` | Advisor where-to-buy, and Components rows in the same catalog |

`fetch-shop-item-index` includes UEX clothing categories (footwear, gloves, hats, jackets, jumpsuits, legwear, shirts, clothing sets, undersuits, eyewear, dresses), medical consumables (medpens and the other pens), and plushies. Leaving a sold category out is how a loot item loses $$$ and cart.

## Every surface

| Surface | $$$ | Cart | Gold chest |
|---|---|---|---|
| Blueprint card (`BlueprintCard.jsx`) | `UexItemActions` | same | `BlueprintLootLocations` |
| Blueprint details (`BlueprintDetailsModal.tsx`) | `UexItemActions` | same | `BlueprintLootLocations` |
| Loot Finder, both tabs (`LootFinderPage.tsx`) | `UexItemActions` via `shopItemForLoot` when the item is sold | same | Already the loot list. Do not add a chest here |
| UEX Lookup buy rows | The page is the shop list, so $$$ stays hidden (`showWhere={false}`) | `UexItemActions` | Not a loot surface |
| Fuzy's Ship Shop part row, Where to Buy, and cart | The $$$ glyph is the Where to Buy control | Ship-shop cart | `BlueprintLootLocations` with `label="Loot Chest"` |

Shared UI only. Do not hardcode a chest allowlist or a second shop list in React.

## Loot Finder chest rules

1. **Add or remove a Loot Finder location** → update `LOCATION_DEFS` in `scripts/lib/parseSiteLoot.mjs`, then bake `game-site-loot.json`. Chest icons follow that bake.
2. **Show the chest** when the blueprint `entityClass` appears in any tracked location (crate loot preferred over NPC-only).
3. **Remove the chest** only when that entity has zero remaining tracked locations after rebake.
4. Lookup helpers live in `src/lib/lootBlueprintLookup.ts`. Keep crate-over-NPC and `_scitem` alias behavior.

## Do not

- Ship one icon onto a surface that already shows another from this set and leave the rest behind
- Skip `fetch-shop-item-index` on a patch that adds shop clothing, armor, guns, food, or drinks
- Skip rebaking `game-site-loot.json` after `LOCATION_DEFS` changes
- Widen the mining-gear bake to armor, clothing, or ships
